On the twenty-eighth day of my internship, I focused on system 
information and Linux logs. I read the relevant sections from the 
Linux book and studied directories such as /var/log, where many 
system and application logs are stored.

I also learned about commands such as uname, df, du, and free. 
These commands can provide information about the operating system, 
disk usage, directory sizes, and memory usage. I reviewed their 
basic purposes and followed examples from the book.

In addition, I learned about journalctl and dmesg as tools for 
examining system and kernel-related information. This gave me 
a better understanding of how Linux administrators can investigate
the state of a system.

